# VFX-SYS-REF: the VFX component's System slot (Asset<VFXSystemAsset>) is drawn as a VFX System picker over the
# content registry's VFXSystem rows (UE TSoftObjectPtr<UNiagaraSystem>), not the Texture2D slot the property
# builder fell into for every asset type without a branch - which asked the .dfx handle as a Texture2D every frame
# (~100 "FindByHandle ... requested as Texture2D" errors) and showed "(missing)" while the effect played.
# The scenario SAVES: `git checkout -- Projects/Desert/Content/Scenes/Starter.desce` after a play.
Дано run Scene "Open Scene Starter.desce"
Когда run Entity "Add to selection Campfire"
Когда state
Тогда 0_details Details shows the VFX component's System = Campfire (not "(missing)"), flames playing; editor.log has 0 Texture2D errors for the .dfx
Когда run Action "Save Scene"
Когда run Scene "Open Scene Starter.desce"
Когда run Entity "Add to selection Campfire"
Когда state
Тогда 1_reopen after the scene is saved and reopened the same System = Campfire, flames playing
